### 3. Google Cloud Storage (GCS) Private Bucket & Asset Service

All user-generated files and sensitive attachments use private Google Cloud Storage buckets with short-lived V4 Signed URLs rather than public bucket links.

* **Bucket Partitioning:**
* `listings/{listingId}/{filename}`: Property and room imagery (served via signed read URLs or CDN-cached read paths).


* `avatars/{userId}/{filename}`: User profile pictures.


* `support/{ticketId}/{filename}`: Private support ticket attachments (strictly authenticated V4 signed URLs expiring in 15 minutes).


* `verifications/{userId}/{filename}`: Temporary staging for clinician license uploads, permanently deleted via `bucket.file(key).delete()` immediately upon admin approval in the verification queue.




* **Signed Upload & Read Endpoints:**
* `POST /api/storage/signed-upload-url`: Validates file MIME type (`image/jpeg`, `image/png`, `image/webp`, `application/pdf`) and size ($\le 10\text{MB}$), returning a V4 `write` signed URL and the `gcs_key`.


* `GET /api/storage/signed-read-url?key=...`: Verifies that the requesting user is authorized (e.g., ticket owner, assigned admin, or booking participant) before generating a 15-minute V4 `read` URL.





